 **Strengths and Limitations:**
-Strengths include efficient precomputation of volumetric lighting and shadows, suitable for static or slowly changing volumes [S1, unofficial]. Limitations include the static nature of the light map, which may not adapt well to dynamic lighting or rapidly changing volume densities without recomputation [S1, unofficial].
+Calculating the lightmap is rather expensive and depends on the amount of lights, the structure of the volume, the resolution of the lightmap, and the step size of the ray during lightmap calculation [S2]. The method is only updated if lighting properties (location, direction) or the volume's optical properties change, which keeps performance high when moving the camera by allowing reuse of the pre-computed lightmap [S2].
 
